# Media policy

- Media binaries (video, audio, images, renders, caches) go to the storage backend
  only: the `cineforge-media` Docker volume (`/data/media`), `var/media` on the host,
  or object storage later. Never commit them; `make check-media` and CI enforce this.
- Store media through `StorageBackend` with keys from `storage_key(...)`
  (`tenants/<tenant>/productions/<id>/<kind>/<file>`).
- Every asset needs provenance and license metadata (`AssetRecord`, `LicenseInfo`):
  source, license, attribution, generator/provider where relevant.
- Rights fail closed: if license or rights are unknown, `RightsGate` blocks the asset.
  Never bypass or weaken the gate to make a demo pass.
- AI-generated content carries the required disclosure in the manifest.
- Test fixtures must be tiny and live under `tests/fixtures/approved/`.
